{# ============================================================ HERO
   Full-bleed photo layer (absolute, right-biased, no frame) with text
   overlaid — rebuilt 2026-08-24 v2 after side-by-side comparison against the
   reference showed the first pass reading as a boxed/contained photo panel
   with too much vertical padding, not the reference's edge-to-edge, tightly
   composed atmosphere. This version: photo is an absolute layer spanning the
   full section height (visible behind the fixed nav at the very top, same
   as the reference), no rounded frame, a wide gradient blend into paper
   instead of a hard edge, and a shorter, denser hero overall.
   Reuses existing site infrastructure rather than inventing new systems —
   the [data-hero-in] GSAP stagger (main.js) for entrance, the same
   overscan-then-transform parallax pattern already used on .facet-field,
   and the existing btn-primary/btn-ghost component classes.
   Eyebrow pill is back, deliberately overriding the earlier Impeccable-driven
   removal — explicit ask this round.
   Every element renders fully visible in plain HTML/CSS first; GSAP only
   choreographs entrance once it has actually loaded (see main.js comment). #}
<section class="relative bg-paper overflow-hidden">
  {# Photo layer — absolute, right-biased, no rounding, no contained box.
     Starts BELOW the fixed nav (top-20/80px — the nav bar's resting-state
     bottom edge measures 69.5px now that the header defaults to a flush
     full-width bar rather than a floating pill, so this is a tight,
     deliberate ~10px margin below that, not a guess) rather than spanning
     the section's full height behind it. Earlier versions let the photo
     extend behind the nav for a more edge-to-edge look, but that meant
     anything near the top of the source photo — specifically the thrown
     caps — could end up partly hidden under the nav depending on viewport
     size, and no amount of crop tuning fixed it reliably at every size.
     Starting below the nav guarantees zero overlap regardless of viewport,
     full stop. #}
  <div class="absolute right-0 top-20 bottom-0 w-full lg:w-[58%] overflow-hidden">
    {# The parallax target is this inner, overscanned (-6% top/bottom)
       wrapper — GSAP moves it within the statically sized, overflow-hidden
       layer so scrolling never exposes a gap (same technique as .facet-field).
       object-position biased right-of-frame: the source photo has an
       "admizz" watermark baked into its top-left corner (known defect,
       docs/RESUME-PROMPT.md) — this crop keeps it out of view without
       needing a re-exported asset. #}
    <div class="hero-photo-parallax absolute -inset-y-[2%] inset-x-0 [&_picture]:contents [&_img]:absolute [&_img]:inset-0 [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover [&_img]:object-[60%_0%] [&_img]:scale-110">
      {% imageEager "src/assets/images/insights/global-opportunities.jpg", "Graduates celebrating, caps thrown in the air", "(min-width: 1024px) 64vw, 100vw" %}
    </div>
    {# Brand-shape watermark — the logo mark's chevron silhouette, simplified
       to a single flat translucent band and layered ON TOP of the photo.
       Blurred: the previous crisp-edged version rendered as a visible hard
       diagonal seam cutting across the faces/arms — looked like a rendering
       bug, not a brand shape. The reference's version reads as soft ambient
       light, not a cut geometric edge, so a real blur (not just low opacity)
       is what actually fixes it. #}
    <svg class="absolute left-1/2 top-[3%] -translate-x-1/2 w-[105%] max-w-[820px] h-auto pointer-events-none blur-2xl" viewBox="0 0 400 260" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M200,5 L340,105 L280,105 L200,50 L120,105 L60,105 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" opacity="0.18"/>
      <path d="M200,120 L390,250 L305,250 L200,175 L95,250 L10,250 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" opacity="0.15"/>
    </svg>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-navy-deep/18 via-transparent to-transparent"></div>
    {# Atmospheric blend into the paper ground — width-controlled via Tailwind's
       gradient stop positions. Narrowed twice now (first pass: via-75%/to-90%;
       this pass: via-38%/to-58%) so most of the photo stays fully saturated —
       only enough coverage to keep the text column clean, not a wash across
       the whole frame. #}
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-paper from-0% via-paper/65 via-22% to-transparent to-58% lg:to-50%"></div>
    {# Top-edge blend — the photo's left edge already fades into the paper
       column (above); the top edge didn't, so where the nav's protective
       gap (see the top-20 comment above) sits over paper it was invisible,
       but the exact same gap sitting over the photo read as a hard, visible
       seam — one gap, two different results depending on contrast. This
       fades the photo's own top ~64px from paper down to fully transparent,
       so it emerges out of the ground the same way the left edge already
       does, rather than starting with a flat line. #}
    <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-16 bg-gradient-to-b from-paper to-transparent"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="shell relative pt-28 pb-3 md:pt-28 md:pb-4">
    <div class="min-h-[320px] md:min-h-[380px] lg:min-h-[430px] flex items-center">
      <div class="relative z-10 max-w-xl">
        {# Dot-grid globe motif, anchored to THIS text column (not the raw
           section) — the earlier version was positioned against the
           full-width section, so on wide viewports the shell centers with a
           growing left margin and the circle rendered mostly off-screen,
           clipped to a meaningless sliver instead of a visible globe. #}
        <svg class="absolute -left-16 -top-14 w-[560px] h-[560px] opacity-[0.16] pointer-events-none hidden lg:block -z-10" viewBox="0 0 560 560" aria-hidden="true">
          <defs>
            <pattern id="hero-dots" width="20" height="20" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
              <circle cx="1.5" cy="1.5" r="1.5" fill="#0B0F69"/>
            </pattern>
            <clipPath id="hero-dots-circle"><circle cx="280" cy="280" r="280"/></clipPath>
          </defs>
          <rect width="560" height="560" fill="url(#hero-dots)" clip-path="url(#hero-dots-circle)"/>
        </svg>

        <span class="eyebrow-pill" data-hero-in>
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-navy"></span>
          Shaping futures. Building possibilities.
        </span>

        {# Hero-scoped heading size, smaller than the shared .text-display-1
           token — that clamp scales to 96px on real desktop widths, and four
           wrapped lines at that size alone ate ~370px, which is what forced
           scrolling on shorter real browser windows. This keeps the same
           fluid/responsive behavior, just with a lower ceiling. #}
        <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-[680px] font-display font-light text-[clamp(1.85rem,1.25rem+2.5vw,3.4rem)] leading-[1.08] text-ink" data-hero-in>
          Transforming education and careers, <em class="italic text-navy font-book">globally.</em>
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-3 text-body-lg text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight" data-hero-in>
          {{ site.description }}
        </p>

        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4" data-hero-in>
          <a href="#ventures" class="btn-primary group">
            Explore our ventures
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" class="transition-transform duration-press ease-signature group-hover:translate-x-0.5"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </a>
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn-ghost">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# Real trust badge — Admizz Education's ICEF accreditation, independently
       verified against ICEF's public API (docs/01-AUDIT.md §2), not a claim
       taken from marketing copy. Anchored to the shell so it aligns with the
       curve below, positioned over the photo layer via z-index. #}
    <a
      href="https://accreditations.icef.com/certificate?id=c8a7212a-a25c-469f-8a7b-2b2f047e8c0c"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      data-hero-in
      data-motion
      class="badge-float absolute bottom-0 right-gutter z-10 flex items-center gap-3 rounded-2xl bg-white/95 backdrop-blur-sm shadow-xl border border-rule px-4 py-3 max-w-[240px] hover:shadow-2xl transition-shadow duration-press ease-signature"
    >
      <span class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-full bg-navy/10 flex items-center justify-center text-navy">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M9 1.5l6 2.25v4c0 4-2.6 6.9-6 8.75-3.4-1.85-6-4.75-6-8.75v-4L9 1.5z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M6.5 9l1.8 1.8L11.5 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </span>
      <span>
        <span class="block text-small font-medium text-ink">ICEF Certified Agency</span>
        <span class="block text-micro text-ink-faint">Admizz Education &middot; Verified</span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>

  {# Curved cap transitioning the paper hero into the navy value band —
     SVG rather than clip-path here since it's bridging two stacked sections,
     not masking a single element; preserveAspectRatio="none" stretches it
     to full width, a standard, responsive technique for this shape.
     The seam bug: the SVG's fill edge anti-aliases against whatever sits
     behind the <svg> element itself, and the old 1px overlap (-mt-px)
     wasn't reliable across zoom levels/DPRs — at some scales a hairline of
     paper showed through as a visible line. Pulling the navy div up by a
     few real pixels (-mt-2) instead of one guarantees the overlap survives
     sub-pixel rounding at any scale. #}
  <div class="relative mt-4 md:mt-5">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 140" preserveAspectRatio="none" class="block w-full h-[32px] md:h-[48px]" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M0,140 L0,45 C 480,135 900,-5 1440,80 L1440,140 Z" fill="#0B0F69"/>
    </svg>
    <div class="bg-navy-deep -mt-2 relative overflow-hidden">
      {# Soft diagonal light sweep — the reference's value band has real
         depth (a lighter-blue glow crossing the upper-left), not a flat
         single navy fill. A large, heavily blurred gradient shape reads as
         ambient light rather than a hard-edged decoration. #}
      <div class="absolute -top-1/2 -left-1/4 w-[75%] h-[220%] bg-gradient-to-br from-navy-soft/55 via-navy/20 to-transparent rotate-12 blur-3xl pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="shell py-6 md:py-7 relative z-10">
        {# Real proof, not decoration — replaces the old "Global Reach / Student
           First / Future Ready" icon strip, which named zero facts. These are
           Admizz Education's own published figures (src/_data/stats.json,
           source: admizzeducation, status: draft), attributed explicitly —
           this is the group site reporting a venture's results, not claiming
           them as the whole group's. Caption pattern borrowed from scaler.com's
           stat block ("Based on the 2026 Scaler career transition assessment")
           — a number is only as credible as who it's attributed to. #}
        <span class="eyebrow-on-navy fade-up">Across Admizz Education</span>
        <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 divide-y divide-navy-on-muted/15 md:divide-y-0 md:divide-x">
          {% for s in stats.headline %}
          <div class="py-4 md:py-0 md:px-8 first:pt-0 md:first:pl-0 last:pb-0 md:last:pr-0 fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 90 }}ms">
            <span class="block font-display font-light text-h3 text-navy-on">{{ s.value }}</span>
            <span class="block mt-1 text-small text-navy-on-muted">{{ s.label }}</span>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-on-muted/70 fade-up">
          Figures published by Admizz Education, as of 2026
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ 01 — THE SHIFT
   New 2026-08-31 (homepage-narrative rebuild). Editorial problem statement,
   the opening move of the new homepage narrative: the world Admizz operates
   in, before Admizz itself.

   2026-08-31 v3: rebuilt against a reference mockup (user-supplied
   screenshot, same copy already written here, richer layout) — added the
   eyebrow, the numbered "what's changing" breakdown, a background world
   map, and a closing link.

   v4 CORRECTION: the first pass reused the hero's plain dot-grid CIRCLE —
   just a blob of dots, not a world map. Rebuilt with a real world outline
   (MIT-licensed, simplemaps.com) driving a CSS mask, but that produced a
   flat RECTANGLE (a map), not a globe.

   v5: tried a round, shaded globe (bleeding off the section's right edge)
   after v4's flat map wasn't right either.

   v6: v5's revert was misread as "delete the map" instead of "go back to
   the dotted world MAP version" — restored the flat dotted world map
   (world-map-dots, same as v4), positioned in the open space to the right
   of the two-column grid so it doesn't overlap the text now that the
   column widths/breakpoint are actually correct (see the placement fixes
   made to this section since v5). The tightened scale (narrower headline
   column, smaller list type/spacing) from v5 stays. #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-paper py-section-sm border-b border-rule">
  <div class="world-map-dots absolute right-8 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-[240px] h-[140px] opacity-[0.42] pointer-events-none hidden xl:block" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="shell relative z-10 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,26rem)_minmax(0,15.5rem)] gap-x-12 gap-y-8 md:items-center">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow fade-up">The Shift</span>
      <p class="mt-3 fade-up font-display font-light text-[clamp(1.5rem,1.1rem+1.8vw,2.3rem)] leading-[1.15] text-ink max-w-[20ch] text-balance" style="animation-delay:60ms">
        Education is more global. Careers are less linear. The skills a job needs can shift <em class="italic text-navy font-book">faster</em> than a degree can be finished.
      </p>
      <span class="block mt-5 w-10 h-px bg-gold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-small text-ink-muted max-w-[36ch] fade-up" style="animation-delay:120ms">
        For most people, the constraint isn&rsquo;t access anymore &mdash; it&rsquo;s knowing what comes next, and having a real way to prepare for it.
        Admizz operates across the three places that question actually gets answered: preparation, education, and work.
      </p>
      <a href="#what-admizz-is" class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-small font-medium text-navy fade-up" style="animation-delay:170ms">
        Explore how we help
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>

    {# The "what's changing" breakdown — three one-line elaborations of the
       headline statement above, not new claims about Admizz itself.
       Dividers between items are a dotted rule (border-dotted), matching
       the reference exactly — NOT the solid .border-rule hairline used
       everywhere else on this page. #}
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 fade-up" style="animation-delay:100ms">
      {% set shifts = [
        { title: "Education is changing.", text: "More options, more destinations, more complexity." },
        { title: "Careers are changing.", text: "Paths aren't fixed anymore. People move, pivot and grow." },
        { title: "Skills are changing.", text: "What you learn today may not be enough tomorrow." }
      ] %}
      {% for s in shifts %}
      <div class="flex gap-3 pt-4 border-t border-dotted border-ink-faint/50 first:pt-0 first:border-t-0">
        <span class="font-mono text-micro tabular-nums text-navy-soft shrink-0">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display font-book text-body text-ink">{{ s.title }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-micro text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ s.text }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ 02 — WHAT ADMIZZ IS
   Positioning section — explains WHY the three businesses are one group,
   not just that they are. Doesn't exist as its own section pre-rebuild;
   was only implied in the hero subhead.

   2026-08-31 v3: rebuilt against the same reference mockup — the three
   venture "preview cards" now live INSIDE this section (photo, number,
   stage, name, one-liner sourced from the venture's own existing
   verticalLine field — nothing new written), plus a small vertical
   pathway diagram on the right, echoing the bigger Ecosystem-pathway
   section further down without duplicating it. This does NOT remove the
   bigger Prepare/Study/Work sticky section below — open question, still
   flagged, on whether that stays once this preview exists. #}
<section id="what-admizz-is" class="bg-paper-sunk py-section-sm border-b border-rule">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,22rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-10 lg:gap-16">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <span class="eyebrow">What Admizz Is</span>
        <h2 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-h1 text-ink max-w-[12ch] text-balance">
          One group. <em class="italic text-navy font-book">Three connected businesses.</em>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up" style="animation-delay:90ms">
        <p class="text-body-lg text-ink-muted leading-relaxed max-w-measure">
          Admizz Institute, Admizz Education and Admizz Workforce Solutions each answer to a different market &mdash; test preparation, international admissions, and workforce development are not the same business, and we don&rsquo;t run them as one.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-muted leading-relaxed max-w-measure">
          What connects them is where they sit on the same line: a test score determines what a university application can achieve; a university decision shapes the career that follows it; a career runs on skills that keep changing after graduation. Most organizations serve one point on that line. Admizz was built to serve more than one of them, without pretending the three are interchangeable.
        </p>
        <a href="/ventures/" class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline">
          Explore our businesses
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# Preview row: 3 venture cards + a mini pathway diagram alongside.
       All 3 photos are user-supplied, explicitly AI-generated images
       (against this project's own "no AI-look imagery" rule in
       docs/00-BRIEF.md §13 — overridden here on explicit instruction,
       same pattern as the ecosystem.jpg exceptions elsewhere, NOT a
       default for future sessions to repeat unprompted). #}
    {% set previewImages = {
      "institute": { file: "preview/institute-preview.jpg", alt: "Student wearing headphones, writing in a notebook" },
      "education": { file: "preview/education-preview.jpg", alt: "Student walking outside a university building with a backpack" },
      "workforce": { file: "preview/workforce-preview.jpg", alt: "Three colleagues talking in a modern office" }
    } %}
    <div class="mt-14 md:mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto] gap-x-10 gap-y-10 items-start fade-up" style="animation-delay:140ms">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-x-8 gap-y-10">
        {% for v in ventures %}
        {% set img = previewImages[v.id] %}
        <div class="venture-preview-card">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
            <span class="font-display font-light text-h3 tabular-nums text-ink-faint">{{ v.index }}</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">{{ v.stage }}</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="mt-1 font-display font-light text-h4 text-ink text-balance">{{ v.name }}</h3>
          <a href="{{ v.href if v.href != '#' else '/ventures/' }}" class="venture-preview-photo mt-4 block relative rounded-lg overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep aspect-[4/5]">
            <div class="absolute inset-0 [&_picture]:contents [&_picture]:block [&_picture]:h-full [&_img]:absolute [&_img]:inset-0 [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover">
              {% image "src/assets/images/" + img.file, img.alt, "(min-width: 1024px) 22vw, (min-width: 640px) 30vw, 80vw" %}
            </div>
          </a>
          <p class="mt-4 text-small text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{{ v.verticalLine }}</p>
          <a href="/ventures/#record-{{ v.id }}" class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline">
            Learn more
            <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      {# Mini pathway — echoes the bigger Ecosystem-pathway section further
         down (same 3 real stages, same gold-dot idiom) at a much smaller
         scale, as a compact index rather than a duplicate of that section. #}
      <div class="hidden lg:flex flex-col items-start gap-6 pl-8 border-l border-rule self-stretch justify-center">
        {% for v in ventures %}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-gold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">{{ v.stage }}</span>
        </div>
        {% if not loop.last %}<span class="w-px h-6 bg-rule ml-[3px]" aria-hidden="true"></span>{% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        <span class="w-px h-6 bg-rule ml-[3px]" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-navy-on-muted/50" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">Opportunity</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ THE ECOSYSTEM (register)
   The former standalone "Statement" section (its own eyebrow+headline+paragraph
   module) was cut here, not relocated — on inspection its copy was a near-verbatim
   restatement of the hero subhead above, with the "three pillars" line it added
   already covered more concretely by the venture-name ticker (real names, not
   category words) and by this register, which explains all three ventures in full. #}
{# No overflow-hidden here, deliberately — it silently breaks position:sticky
   on any descendant (an ancestor's overflow other than visible forces sticky
   to compute against that ancestor instead of the viewport), which is
   exactly what happened the first time this was written: the sticky photo
   below just scrolled away instead of staying put. #}
<section id="ventures" class="bg-paper py-section">
  <div class="shell">
    {# Subtitle stacked directly under the heading, not split off to the far
       right of the shell — that put real distance between a line and the
       heading it supports, reading as orphaned rather than connected. #}
    <div class="max-w-[42rem] fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow">Prepare / Study / Work</span>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink">Three businesses. Real ground covered.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight">
        Each of the three below solves a different problem, for a different audience &mdash; not three steps of one script.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {# Deliberately outside .shell — the sticky-photo/text grid inside this
     partial breaks full-bleed to the viewport edge on its photo side. #}
  {% include "partials/ecosystem-journey.njk" %}
</section>

{# ============================================================ 04 — OUR EXPERTISE
   New 2026-08-31. Editorial index, not six identical cards — reuses the
   exact .academic-network-row expand/collapse idiom (Alpine collapse,
   already registered in main.js) for a second instance of the same pattern
   rather than inventing a new one. Four categories, not six: verified
   against ventures.json's actual descriptions — test prep, admissions
   counseling, visa/scholarship support, and workforce development are the
   only capabilities with real copy behind them anywhere in this repo.
   Career Development and Learning & Training (from the brief's example
   list) are NOT included — no distinct, verifiable service exists for
   either beyond what Workforce Development already covers. #}
<section class="bg-paper py-section-sm md:py-section border-t border-rule">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="max-w-[42rem] fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow">Our Expertise</span>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink">What Admizz actually does.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 fade-up" style="animation-delay:90ms" x-data="{ open: 0 }">
      {% set expertise = [
        { index: "01", name: "Test Preparation", venture: "Admizz Institute", text: "Structured preparation for IELTS, PTE, SAT, GRE and GMAT — the tests that determine what an application can achieve before it's even submitted." },
        { index: "02", name: "Admissions & Counseling", venture: "Admizz Education", text: "Choosing a destination, shortlisting institutions, and building an application around a student's actual academic profile, not a template." },
        { index: "03", name: "Visa & Scholarship Support", venture: "Admizz Education", text: "Guidance through visa applications and scholarship opportunities — the practical steps that stand between an offer and actually enrolling." },
        { index: "04", name: "Workforce Development", venture: "Admizz Workforce Solutions", text: "Supported employment, job coaching and career-transition guidance, focused on vocational rehabilitation for individuals with disabilities." }
      ] %}
      {% for e in expertise %}
      <div>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="academic-network-row"
          @click="open = open === {{ loop.index0 }} ? null : {{ loop.index0 }}"
          :aria-expanded="open === {{ loop.index0 }} ? 'true' : 'false'"
          aria-controls="expertise-panel-{{ loop.index0 }}"
        >
          <span class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-small tabular-nums text-ink-faint">{{ e.index }}</span>
            <span class="font-display font-light text-h4 text-ink">{{ e.name }}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="flex items-center gap-4">
            <span class="hidden md:inline font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">{{ e.venture }}</span>
            <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"
              class="academic-network-chevron text-ink-faint transition-transform duration-press ease-signature"
              :class="open === {{ loop.index0 }} ? 'rotate-180' : ''">
              <path d="M2.5 4.5L6 8l3.5-3.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </span>
        </button>
        <div id="expertise-panel-{{ loop.index0 }}" x-show="open === {{ loop.index0 }}" x-collapse x-cloak>
          <p class="pb-5 pt-1 md:pl-11 text-body text-ink-muted leading-relaxed max-w-measure-tight">{{ e.text }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ 05 — THE ADMIZZ ECOSYSTEM
   New 2026-08-31. The conceptual pathway (Potential -> Opportunity),
   distinct from the "One Ecosystem" business pitch above despite the
   similar name — GSAP/CSS only, no Three.js: a horizontal (desktop) /
   vertical (mobile) node line with staggered fade-up reveal per node is
   sufficient to carry this idea; a WebGL layer wasn't judged to add
   anything a typographic diagram doesn't already say. Two real business
   stages (Preparation/Education/Work map to the three ventures) sit beside
   three narrative stages (Potential, Skills, Opportunity) that are NOT
   claimed as Admizz services — they're the surrounding context the three
   real businesses operate inside.

   2026-08-31 v2: applying the Taste Skill redesign checklist to the flat
   repetition problem — grain texture instead of an empty flat navy block,
   and the three REAL nodes now lift into raised panels (real depth via
   negative margin + a soft, hue-matched shadow, radius 12px per CLAUDE.md's
   "panels" tier) while the three narrative nodes stay flush/minimal — the
   asymmetry IS the point: it visually separates "what Admizz operates" from
   "the context around it" instead of six identical ticks in a row. Real
   nodes link to their /ventures/ record instead of sitting inert. #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep py-section">
  {% include "partials/grain-texture.njk" %}
  <div class="shell relative z-10">
    <div class="max-w-[46rem] fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow-on-navy">The Admizz Ecosystem</span>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-h1 text-navy-on max-w-[18ch] text-balance">
        From potential <em class="italic text-navy-accent font-book">to opportunity.</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-body-lg text-navy-on-muted max-w-measure">
        Preparation, education and work aren't separate markets to us &mdash; they're three points on the same line a person actually walks. Admizz operates at three of them; the line runs further than that on both ends.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ecosystem-path mt-16 md:mt-20 fade-up" style="animation-delay:120ms">
      {% set pathNodes = [
        { label: "Potential", detail: "Where a person starts.", real: false },
        { label: "Preparation", detail: "Admizz Institute", real: true, href: "/ventures/#record-institute" },
        { label: "Education", detail: "Admizz Education", real: true, href: "/ventures/#record-education" },
        { label: "Skills", detail: "What a career now runs on.", real: false },
        { label: "Work", detail: "Admizz Workforce Solutions", real: true, href: "/ventures/#record-workforce" },
        { label: "Opportunity", detail: "Where the line leads.", real: false }
      ] %}
      <div class="ecosystem-path-line relative hidden md:block h-px bg-navy-on-muted/25 mb-8" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="ecosystem-path-track grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-6 gap-x-4 gap-y-10 md:gap-x-3">
        {% for n in pathNodes %}
        {% if n.real %}
        <a href="{{ n.href }}" class="ecosystem-path-node ecosystem-path-node-real group relative fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ 160 + loop.index0 * 70 }}ms">
          <span class="ecosystem-path-dot absolute left-4 -top-[27px] md:-top-[35px] block w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-on">{{ n.label }}</span>
          <span class="mt-1.5 block text-small text-navy-on-muted">{{ n.detail }}</span>
          <span class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-micro font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-accent opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100">
            <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </span>
        </a>
        {% else %}
        <div class="ecosystem-path-node relative pt-6 fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ 160 + loop.index0 * 70 }}ms">
          <span class="ecosystem-path-dot absolute left-0 top-0 block w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-navy-on-muted/40" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="block font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-on-muted">{{ n.label }}</span>
          <span class="mt-1.5 block text-small text-navy-on-muted/60">{{ n.detail }}</span>
        </div>
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ 06 — WHAT WE BELIEVE
   Revived and rewritten from the disabled "Statement band" (previously
   wrapped in {% if false %}, hidden 2026-08-25). Same navy-band visual
   language, new job: a real point of view, not a generic mission quote.
   Three concise principles, each one sentence — deliberately not slogans
   ("unlock your potential" etc, banned by the brief). Grounded in what's
   already established across ventures.json/marketContext.json, not new
   claims.

   2026-08-31 v2: was an equal 3-column grid — the exact "sameness" pattern
   flagged as flat/templated. Reworked into an asymmetric 5/7-column split:
   principle 01 gets a raised, larger panel of its own (the one this project
   treats as foundational — everything else follows from taking preparation
   seriously); 02 and 03 stack smaller beside it. Grain texture replaces the
   section's previous plain gradient-only surface. #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy py-section-sm">
  {% include "partials/grain-texture.njk" %}
  <div class="absolute -bottom-1/3 -right-1/4 w-[70%] h-[200%] bg-gradient-to-tl from-navy-accent/40 via-navy-soft/15 to-transparent -rotate-12 blur-3xl pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="shell relative">
    <span class="eyebrow-on-navy fade-up">What We Believe</span>
    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-6 md:gap-8 items-start">
      <div class="belief-panel belief-panel-featured md:col-span-5 fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">
        <span class="block font-mono text-small tabular-nums text-navy-accent">01</span>
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-h2 text-navy-on max-w-[14ch] text-balance">Preparation is not a formality.</h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-body text-navy-on-muted leading-relaxed max-w-[34ch]">A test score or an application isn&rsquo;t a checkbox &mdash; it&rsquo;s the thing that decides which doors are actually open.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-7 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 md:gap-8 md:mt-10">
        {% set beliefs = [
          { title: "Education should lead somewhere.", text: "A university choice is a career decision made early. We treat it as one, not as an admissions transaction." },
          { title: "Skills close gaps services alone don't.", text: "Access to a program is a start. What a person can actually do with it afterward is the part that's easy to overlook." }
        ] %}
        {% for b in beliefs %}
        <div class="belief-panel fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 90 + 170 }}ms">
          <span class="block font-mono text-small tabular-nums text-navy-accent">0{{ loop.index + 1 }}</span>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-h3 text-navy-on max-w-[16ch] text-balance">{{ b.title }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-small text-navy-on-muted leading-relaxed max-w-[32ch]">{{ b.text }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% include "partials/academic-network.njk" %}

